me-regulated anion channels in endothelial cells</article-title><source>Br J Pharmacol</source><year>1999</year><volume>128</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bjp.0702770</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Droogmans G, Maertens C, Prenen J, Nilius B (1999) Sulphonic acid derivatives as probes of pore properties of volume-regulated anion channels in endothelial cells. Br J Pharmacol 128:35&#x02013;40 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10498832</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gopel</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanno</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Barg</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Weng</surname><given-names>XG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gromada</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rorsman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulation of glucagon release in mouse &#x003b1;-cells by K<sub>ATP</sub> channels and inactivation of TTX-sensitive Na<sup>+</sup> channels</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>528</volume><fpage>509</fpage><lpage>520</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1469-7793.2000.00509.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Gopel SO, Kanno T, Barg S, Weng XG, Gromada J, Rorsman P (2000) Regulation of glucagon release in mouse &#x003b1;-cells by KATP channels and inactivation of TTX-sensitive Na+ channels. J Physiol 528:509&#x02013;520 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11060128</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grinstein</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Clarke</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothstein</surnam